<p dir=3D"ltr">What this fixes:</p>
<ul dir=3D"ltr">
<li><strong>One query</strong>, with the sum translated to SQL (fixes issue=
s 1 and 4).</li>
<li><strong>No tracking</strong> (issue 3).</li>
<li><strong>Bounded result</strong> via paging (issue 2).</li>
<li><strong>Only needed columns</strong> (issue 5).</li>
<li><strong>DTO boundary</strong>, no entity mutation (issues 6 and 7).</li=
>
<li><strong>Cancellation</strong> supported (issue 8).</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir=3D"ltr" aria-level=3D"5">Things to verify before production</h3>
<ul dir=3D"ltr">
<li><strong>Check the generated SQL</strong> (via <code dir=3D"ltr">ToQuery=
String()</code> or logging) to confirm the <code dir=3D"ltr">Sum</code> tra=
nslates to a single query. Translation behavior can vary with provider and =
model, and I haven=E2=80=99t assumed a specific provider.</li>
<li><strong>Index the foreign key</strong> on the items table (the order ID=
 column) so the correlated sum is efficient.</li>
<li><strong>Decide on empty <code dir=3D"ltr">Items</code></strong>: <code =
dir=3D"ltr">Sum</code> over an empty collection returns 0 for <code dir=3D"=
ltr">decimal</code>, which is probably what you want, but confirm.</li>
<li><strong>Don=E2=80=99t call this with an unbounded page size</strong>: c=
ap <code dir=3D"ltr">pageSize</code> at the caller or service level.</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"ltr">If you can share the <code dir=3D"ltr">Order</code>/<code di=
r=3D"ltr">OrderItem</code> classes and how the context is registered (lazy =
loading, tracking behavior), I can tell you definitively which failure mode=
 in issue 1 applies.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=3D"m=
